            "limitations": [],
            "material_ready": true,
            "material_usefulness": "direct",
            "outline_action": "Incorporate the Zhang et al. retrospective cohort findings into the review's section on 'Timing of Antibiotic Exposure.' Highlight the distinction between pre-only (non-significant long-term effect after adjustment) and post-only (significant 27% increased mortality risk) exposure. Use the tumor-specific subgroup data (significant in Head & Neck, RCC, Breast; non-significant in Lung, Melanoma) to discuss heterogeneity in susceptibility. Note the limitation that these are observational associations without direct microbiome validation.",
            "outline_action_recovered_by_policy": false,
            "remaining_gap": "The gap remains partially unmet regarding the specific association with treatment response (e.g., ORR, DCR) and progression-free survival (PFS); this study only reports Overall Survival (OS). Additionally, while timing is addressed, the specific mechanisms linking antibiotic exposure to outcomes remain inferred rather than directly measured due to lack of microbiome data.",
            "remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy": false,
